WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.100
In order to counter
the strange phenomena

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.770
occurring at Yuasa High School,

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:08.440
Monk and the others each
began their exorcisms,

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.440
but to virtually no effect.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.450
She's cursed me!

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.950
On the contrary, the incidents
just kept escalating.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:22.790
That woman didn't look
at me even once.

00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:25.460
Only Naru...

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.790
This is a zuzhou!

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:31.130
Someone has cast an enmi spell
against a person at this school,

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:35.130
and evil spirits are appearing
to the ones being cursed.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.140
Masako and Ayako both say
that the culprit is Kasai-san,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.810
but I don't think so.
Afterward, just as Naru predicted,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.150
hitogata that were used for
the zuzhou hex were found

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:49.480
in the places that were
connected to the incidents.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:52.490
All that was left was to find
the culprit who made them,

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.530
and the case would be solved,
or so we thought...

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.930
I heard it appeared again.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.940
They say it was the same one
as Yoshino-sensei's.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:52.020
It's a curse.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.610
No doubt about it, I'm sure it's her.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.280
Kasai Chiaki did this.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.610
No!

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.580
Take care of her, John.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.960
Right. You guys take care, too.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:25.300
Wouldn't it be best if we just
caught this Kasai girl right away?

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:27.180
If we don't,
our own lives are in danger!

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:30.640
You're wrong!
Kasai-san isn't the culprit!

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:34.980
Are you still saying that?
Then, who else could it be!?

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.990
W-well... I don't know...

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:42.660
Whoever the culprit may be,
this was a warning.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.990
A warning?

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.990
The culprit is targeting myself
and Hara-san as a message,

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:50.330
telling us not to stick our noses
into this case any further.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:55.330
A message!? Masako was pushed
down the stairs! And you, Naru!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.340
Yeah, I'm not fishing
for gratitude or anything,

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:03.010
but if I hadn't jumped in when I did,
who knows what would have happened?

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.680
Assuming that the culprit effectively
didn't care if we lost our lives,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.020
so long as their secondary goal
in delivering a warning was achieved,

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:14.690
it will be difficult to find
the truth behind this case.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.980
The culprit's targets
were Yoshino-sensei,

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.570
the students who sat at that
desk in 2nd Year, 5th Class,

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:22.030
who met with train accidents,
one after the next,

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:23.700
and the track team.

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.370
We actually did find hitogata in the desk
and track team room in question.

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.870
It's clear that the culprit was
after someone connected to them.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:37.540
We are aware that we are at risk.
We will continue to work,

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.380
to make sure that the situation
doesn't get any worse.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.720
Me, Lin, and Mai will look into
who is connected

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:44.720
to the desk and the track team.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.050
Monk, you and Matsuzaki-san
will continue

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.510
to search for hitogata throughout
the school. Got it?

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.480
- R-right.
- Right.

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:56.400
We wind up doing the manual labor!?

00:04:56.400 --> 00:05:00.400
He just seems to use us
however he wants to, doesn't he?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.740
Aww, man, my nails are ruined!

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:06.200
What's the big idea?

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.410
Say, Monk...

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.210
What?

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:22.760
Long hair...

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:26.430
Isn't that the Kasai girl that Mai
and the others were talking about?

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:31.760
What that seat has in common
with the track team, huh?

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.100
Who's the first one
to sit in that seat?

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:38.100
1st term... I forget.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.770
2nd Term, it was a girl
named Murayama-san.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.780
From a period of when until when?

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.780
Let's see... the first seating change
was halfway through September...

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.450
At our school, we change seating
on the 15th of each month, see?

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:55.450
So, it was from July 15th
to September 14th,

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.790
with summer vacation in the middle.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.130
When did she have her accident?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.800
Two or three days before
the seating change, I think.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:07.470
I see. So that means that
the culprit placed the hitogata

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:12.810
in the desk sometime between July
15th and September 11th or 12th.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.140
Hitogata?

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:17.810
The accidents started happening
about halfway through September,

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.150
The person before Murayama-san
was probably not connected.

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.150
She must have done something to earn
the ire of the culprit during that time.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:27.820
Ire?

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:30.320
They harbored at least
that much of a grudge.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.490
The culprit had to have known
Murayama-san, or at least her face.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.160
Which means that we can rule
out teachers not over her class,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.170
and the other students in that grade.

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:45.170
I wouldn't say that. We have unfamiliar
liaison teachers that come in,

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:48.170
and other students come
over for club meetings, too,

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:50.840
so many people know Murayama-san.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.510
What's the matter?

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:58.850
During the Kasai Panic...

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:03.190
we dragged Kasai-san over
to our classroom a number of times,

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.530
and had her show us her spoon-bending.

00:07:06.530 --> 00:07:09.200
One time, Murayama-san said...

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.530
Would you knock it off, already!?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:13.870
How long are you going to
go on squawking about that!?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.540
Psychic powers? It's really
just bunkum, isn't it!?

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:24.540
And that's not all. Murayama-san also
went to complain to Ubusuna-sensei.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.550
Ubusuna-sensei?

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:31.550
Ubusuna-sensei knows an awful lot
about psychic powers and stuff,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:35.220
and I've gone to ask her about it
a number of times before, myself.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.560
Spoon-bending would be included
under the classification of PK-ST.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:45.560
There's also PK-MT, the willpower
to affect objects in motion,

00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:51.900
say, by wishing that a rolled die
comes up 2, and then it actually does.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.910
These are things that most people
have the latent ability to do.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:08:00.250
That's why I think that after
the whole school got caught up

00:08:00.250 --> 00:08:04.920
in psychic power, she kept
sticking up for Kasai-san.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:10.050
And Murayama-san went to complain
to this same Ubusuna-sensei.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:13.260
Mm-hmm. The teacher said
she couldn't say anything,

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:14.930
because it would just stir things up.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:19.600
That's when the other teachers
and the PTA started making a big scene.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:25.270
So, Murayama-san was the first person
to reject psychic powers, then?

00:08:25.270 --> 00:08:28.940
Oh, now that you mention it,
the track team were also deniers.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.610
And Yoshino-sensei
is their adviser, too.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:38.280
So I think none of the team members
believed in psychic powers, either.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.130
True enough, everyone that
Takahashi-san said had come out

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:51.760
against Kasai have now all
come to some harm.

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:55.300
So that would mean...

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:59.640
The likelihood that Kasai-san
is the culprit just went up.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.640
J-just a minute!

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.980
Zuzhou do not work if just
anyone were to do them.

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:07.980
Only those who are knowledgeable
about psychic powers,

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:10.610
or who have had special training
can perform them.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:16.990
B-but you said that Kasai-san's
psychic power was unstable, Naru!

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.320
Didn't you?

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.990
Do you think that someone unstable
like that could work a zuzhou?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.410
Yeah, that is true, huh?

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:29.670
Zuzhou come from
the Yin-yang Tao, right?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:35.010
So, a yin-yang master
could dispel them.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.010
I see. So he's a yin-yang master...

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.680
When I told Kasai-san that you
were a yin-yang master, Naru,

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.350
she got a surprised look on her face.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:47.020
I'm a yin-yang master?
Where did you get that?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.020
Eh? You're not?

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:49.690
No, I'm not.

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:54.030
B-but during that case before,
you used a hitogata, didn't you!?

00:09:54.030 --> 00:09:58.030
Monk said that was something that
only a yin-yang master could do!

00:09:58.030 --> 00:10:01.370
Lin was the one who made that.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:04.040
You mean, Lin-san
is a yin-yang master?

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:07.040
Yeah, you could say that.

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.710
Even so, it still remains that
the likelihood has gone up, huh?

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:14.710
That Kasai-san is the culprit?

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:17.380
If she thought that
I was a yin-yang master,

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.720
and was afraid that I could
dispel her zuzhou, then yes.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:26.140
But, just supposing now, she did it
unconsciously, without even knowing...

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:31.400
Not possible. Enmi is an art
that actively curses the subject.

00:10:31.400 --> 00:10:33.070
In that case...

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.030
No, it's not right!

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:38.070
Kasai-san is not the sort
of person who would do this!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.410
Is this your intuition again, Mai?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.410
Kasai-san is not the culprit.

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:54.750
Very well, I'll trust in you
one more time, Mai.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.760
I'm going to go look something up.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:00.090
Mai, you go help the others
search for hitogata.

00:11:02.760 --> 00:11:05.260
Uh-huh, all right!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.110
What!?

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.440
You've gotta be kidding me!

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:19.110
B-but Monk, you were the one who
had it wrong in the first place.

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:21.110
Making hitogata
and performing purifications,

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:24.450
and now, spotting this zuzhou-
everything we've seen

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:27.790
led us to think he's obviously
a yin-yang master, doesn't it?

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:31.580
Actually, it seems that
Lin-san is the yin-yang master.

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.920
Aww, it feels like we've been cheated.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:37.800
I've put up with his impudent
attitude all this time, thinking,

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:41.800
"what else could I do?
He's a yin-yang master."

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:43.800
Ubusuna-sensei...

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:49.810
Um, I heard that
Hara Masako-san had gotten hurt.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.140
Yes. She fell down some stairs.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:54.150
Is she all right?

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.480
It doesn't appear
to be life-threatening,

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.820
but if she had landed any differently,
it could have been much worse.

00:11:59.820 --> 00:12:02.820
I wish you'd opened your eyes and taken
a good look at this psychic girl

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:05.490
you're standing up for,
before you'd gotten this concerned.

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:06.490
Ayako!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:11.290
I knew it. You people think that
this is Kasai-san's fault, too, huh?

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.170
Of course we do.

00:12:13.170 --> 00:12:15.500
We can't say for certain
that it isn't, after all.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.840
Right now, she's very frightened.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.260
There's no telling what she
will do if this keeps up.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.510
You're not saying she might
commit suicide, or something?

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:29.520
I'm not so sure.
She was checking us out earlier.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.640
Maybe she was trying to decide
who to place a curse on next.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.850
Are you?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.520
I'm sorry!

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:38.020
I'm really sorry.

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:44.860
I'm not like them. I mean, I don't
think that Kasai-san is the culprit.

00:12:44.860 --> 00:12:49.540
I'm not sure of the reason,
but I can feel it.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.200
You feel it?

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.540
There's a voice in my heart...

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:56.210
Kasai-san isn't the culprit.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:59.880
I can't call it anything more
than an instinct,

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.550
but still, I'd like
to believe my instinct.

00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:06.890
What's your name?

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:08.220
Taniyama Mai.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:11.180
Thank you, Taniyama-san.

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.060
I'm sure that Kasai-san
will be thrilled.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:20.570
If possible, I'd like for you
others to let this matter rest.

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:24.190
I don't want Kasai-san
to be run down any further.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.240
What does she mean,
she wants us to let it rest?

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:32.240
How could she not claim responsibility
if something even worse happens?

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.910
It could be our turn, next.

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.420
Nothing here.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:46.090
For now, I've looked
everywhere that stands out.

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:54.140
"Keep out"

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:00.110
A child's voice?

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.940
Is someone there? Hello?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:14.120
Where are you? Answer me!

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.630
Don't cry! Answer me!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.290
Please!

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.300
What are you doing in there?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.310
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:42.980
Big Sister is coming down
right now, okay?

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.320
Mai!

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.990
What are you doing?

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.990
There's a child that fell down here.

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:55.330
A child?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:59.000
Yeah, there's a knapsack over there.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.340
The knapsack is gone...

00:15:03.340 --> 00:15:03.750
Mai!

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:06.670
I-I'm all right.

00:15:25.020 --> 00:15:30.360
Listen to me. Calmly put your foot
on the ladder. Can you do that?

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:32.030
Mm-hmm.

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:37.370
I'm falling!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.040
Yow...

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.380
I fell down the well
on that last investigation, too.

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:51.050
Why does this always happen to me?

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.050
Are you all right?

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.390
Naru, you fell, too?

00:15:56.390 --> 00:16:00.060
If you had let go of my hand,
I wouldn't have had to.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:05.060
S-sorry. I didn't expect
the ladder to break.

00:16:05.060 --> 00:16:07.730
S-say, help is going
to be coming soon, right?

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:10.070
Did you tell anyone
that you were coming here?

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.070
Mm-mm.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.400
Me, either.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:16.070
Hey! Somebody!

00:16:17.410 --> 00:16:20.410
What were you doing
in a place like this?

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.750
Well, I heard a child crying,

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.250
and when I went looking,
I saw a girl down here.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.090
She's not here.

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.430
Of course not. Why didn't
I think it was strange?

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.760
The bottom was pitch-black,
and I couldn't see anything,

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.770
yet I could clearly
make out the girl...

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:44.100
So that means they're
finally after you, too, Mai.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:47.770
How can you be so calm,
down in a place like this!?

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:51.110
What's worse, it's going
to be night soon.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:55.450
That's right. Once it gets dark, that
woman or the child might appear again.

00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:59.450
And of all people, I'm down here
with the coldest man on earth!

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.120
Okay, so it's my own fault
that he fell down here,

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:07.790
but at a time like this, he could be
a little encouraging, or comforting.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.800
Hold on. If you
think about it, this is...

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:14.800
...a world for just the two of us!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.800
Doing better now?

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.140
I am.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:24.140
That look on his face now was
like the Naru in my dreams...

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.810
You could tell I was feeling better?

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:27.480
I can tell.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:31.480
Mai, you get depressed first,
then you get mad.

00:17:31.480 --> 00:17:34.490
Once that happens, your mood improves,
and you turn more positive.

00:17:34.490 --> 00:17:36.820
You can tell that so plainly?

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.820
It shows on your face, after all.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.830
I-it does? Oh, my...

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:45.160
Mai, want me to introduce
you to my pet?

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:47.580
Come on out here.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:52.840
Y-you don't mean that
¥500 coin, do you?

00:17:55.510 --> 00:17:57.840
Now you've made fun of him,
and he hid himself, didn't he?

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.510
No he didn't, he's in your hand, Naru!

00:18:00.510 --> 00:18:01.850
Where?

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.190
There he is.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:11.520
How'd you do that?
Let me see it!

00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:12.860
Here.

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:18.200
Huh? Geez, you didn't even toss it!

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:21.660
Looks like he got scared
and hid when you yelled, Mai.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:25.540
I did not yell!

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:28.210
Oh, this is where he is.

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:29.880
You're good at magic.

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:31.880
You think it's magic?

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:33.210
Isn't it?

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:34.340
No, it isn't.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:36.210
I-it talked!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.220
You wouldn't be afraid
of Mai, would you?

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.220
Mm-hmm.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:40.890
You don't have to be afraid.

00:18:40.890 --> 00:18:43.390
Mai isn't as scary
as she looks, after all.

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:44.560
Really?

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:49.560
Amazing! This is that
ventriloquism thingie, isn't it?

00:18:49.560 --> 00:18:53.570
Even knowing that as I watch, it really
does look like the coin is talking.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.570
Say, do some more of that.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.570
I can't do anything more
complicated than that right now.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.570
Are you hurt somewhere?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.580
I don't have any gear.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:07.910
Maybe it's because it's dark,
but he looks pale.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:16.590
Don't worry. Once everyone gets
back together, and I'm not there,

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:21.590
Lin at least will come looking,
even if the others don't.

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:27.930
What's wrong?

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:31.270
Whatever happens, stay close to me,
and keep calm.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.940
What's that?

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.620
It's all right.

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.950
It's not going to be all
that much stronger after one day.

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.120
Don't panic and get yourself killed.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.300
What's that?

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.970
Oh, no...

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.640
It's all right.

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.980
Naru...

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:21.320
Still... somebody...

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:28.330
Monk... Ayako... anybody, help!

00:20:33.620 --> 00:20:36.670
W-what? Why did it suddenly?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:41.010
Naru, are you there!?

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:44.680
Lin-san!

00:20:44.680 --> 00:20:46.640
That was quick.

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:50.020
We need a rope or a ladder,
and a flashlight.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.350
I'm impressed that there
are this many of them.

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:54.850
Still, we never thought
to look down the manhole.

00:20:54.850 --> 00:20:57.360
"Taniyama Mai"
Still, we never thought
to look down the manhole.

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:58.360
Still, we never thought
to look down the manhole.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:00.690
Mai...

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:05.030
Me, Hara-san, and Yoshino-sensei's
hitogata were there.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:07.370
Then our names weren't among them?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.700
That's kind of a relief.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:12.700
It's like saying we're
beneath their notice.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:14.370
All that remains is
to flush these hitogata

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.370
down the river, or burn them up,

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:18.880
and the power of the enmi
will be quashed.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:23.050
But do you think that will
make the culprit give up?

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.380
We don't even know who
the culprit is.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:28.390
I'm telling you,
it's not Kasai-san, okay?

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:31.720
Well, I'm not so sure about that.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:36.390
Hey, Naru-chan, what's wrong?

00:21:39.400 --> 00:21:42.400
Are you not feeling well, Naru-chan?

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.420
N-Naru...

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:06.590
Naru!!

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:48.530
Next time: File 3,
"The After School Hexer" #4
